  "notes": "Official JBU plans index (catoid=33, 2025-2026 catalog, labeled Archived Catalog). Transcribed 2026-10-01 from the official PDF. Plan titled 'B.S. IN COMPUTER SCIENCE MAJOR w/ Minors: Sample 4-Year Plan (2025-2026)', Revised 2/21/25; stamped catalog_year 2025-2026 honestly. Genuine catalog discrepancy preserved: Junior Spring prints 14 hours but the five listed courses sum to 12 (BBL 2022 2 + Whole Person Wellness Elective* 2 + EN 3222 2 + CS 3533 3 + Minor/Elective* 3); EN 3222 is kept at 2 hours per the JBU course-code pattern, consistent with the pre-existing B.S. Artificial Intelligence seed. The Junior year header prints 32 hours while 18+12=30. total_credits is the sequenced sum (121). Electives marked with * in the source ('See the Academic Catalog for the list of classes that meet this criteria') are modeled as choice placeholders. The plan footer reads '(Minors as necessary to complete the minimum of 120 hours total) - please turn over the page for Minor courses'. Minors for BS - Computer Science (opt for at least one of the following Minors, 18 hours; documented from page 2): Artificial Intelligence minor: CS 1233 OOP, CS 2243 Data Structures, CS 3643 Artificial Intelligence, CS 3773 Big Data & Cloud Computing, CS 4023 Advanced Computing Concepts, CYB 7103 Cybersecurity Foundations. Game Design Minor: ART 1123 Computer Graphics, CS 1113 Introduction to Computing, CS 3333 Game Design 1, CS 3343 Game Design 2, EGL 2273 Introduction to Creative Writing, plus Any One of ART 2273 3D Modeling for Designers & Illustrators / ART 2613 Digital Illustration. Full Stack Development: CS 1233 OOP, CS 2423 Web Applications, CYB 7103 Cybersecurity Foundations (Online), CS3683 Advance Java Programming, CS3473 Advanced Web Applications, CS4083 Software Testing & Quality Assurance. Data Analytics: Any One of CS 1113 Intro to Computing / CS 1233 Object Oriented Programming; Any One of BUS 2193 Business Statistics / MTH 1003 Introduction to Statistics / MTH 2103 Applied Statistics for Scientists; Any Two of DAT 3113 Basic Data Analytics / DAT 4253 Business Decision Modeling & Predictive Analysis / DAT 4313 Data Visualization; Any Two of CS 2243 Data Structures and Algorithms / CS 3363 Database Design / CS 3643 Artificial Intelligence / CS 3773 Big Data & Cloud Computing. Cybersecurity: CS 1113 Intro to Computing; Any ONE of BUS 2193 Business Statistics (On Campus and Online) / MTH 1003 Introduction to Statistics (On Campus and Online) / MTH 2103 Applied Statistics for Scientists (On Campus); Any FOUR of CYB 7103 Cybersecurity Foundations (Online), CYB 7223 Network and Cloud Security (Online), CYB 7233 Information Technology Risk Management (Online), CYB 7243 Web Application Security (Online), CYB 7433 Incident Management (Online). ",
